# homeDX Non-Code Project Work

When files under `work/` are in play, treat the task as **project work outside the codebase** (market, meetings, roadmap, partnerships, brand, finance, notes, etc.)—not app engineering—unless the user explicitly asks for code changes.

## Grounding

- Start from [`work/product-brief.md`](work/product-brief.md): homeDX is a **software accessory** to the **Cube** reader (Bluetooth → on-device evaluation → backend storage → display), with a **care pathway** after positive results (specialist booking + Daily.co video). Do not describe the app as performing the diagnostic measurement itself.
- Prefer real product capabilities over aspirational features. Check [`docs/APP_FUNCTIONALITIES.md`](docs/APP_FUNCTIONALITIES.md) if unsure what ships today.
- Engineering setup and API docs live under `docs/`; do not duplicate them into `work/`.

## How to work

- Prefer **writing or updating files** under `work/` over chat-only answers. Use the map in [`work/README.md`](work/README.md).
- Put content in the right area: `work/strategy/` (market/competitors), `work/meetings/`, `work/roadmap/`, `work/partnerships/`, `work/brand/`, `work/finance/`, or `work/notes/` as catch-all.
- Use `_template.md` files when present; name meetings and analyses with `YYYY-MM-DD-…` where helpful.
- Cite sources for market/competitor claims (`work/strategy/sources/`). Do not invent market sizes, CE marks, or clinical performance—leave TBD or mark unverified.
- Do not commit secrets (credentials, bank details, private personal data) into git.

## Regulatory / claims

- When work touches medical claims, disease performance, or CE status, **flag risk** and point to [`.cursor/rules/mdr-compliance.mdc`](.cursor/rules/mdr-compliance.mdc) / [`docs/regulatory/`](docs/regulatory/).
- Do **not** invent clinical claims for homeDX or others. Use only public, sourced statements.

## Stay out of the way of coding

- Do not refactor `backend/` or `frontend/` as part of `work/` tasks.
- Do not move regulatory QMS content into `work/`.
